    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\n'Woodview' presents a rare opportunity to create a truly exceptional home in one of Dublin's most sought-after coastal locations. Set on a secluded site of approximately 0.25 acres, this unique offering combines the tranquillity and privacy of a mature woodland setting with the convenience of excellent transport links and the outstanding lifestyle for which Howth is renowned.\n\nBenefiting from full planning permission for a striking contemporary detached residence extending to approximately 381 sq.m. (4,101 sq.ft.), purchasers have the opportunity to realise a bespoke, energy-efficient home without the uncertainty, time and expense typically associated with the planning process. Whether creating a forever family home, downsizing locally without compromising on quality or location, or relocating to Ireland from overseas, Woodview offers an increasingly rare chance to build a home tailored to your own vision in an established and prestigious setting.\n\nThe approved development provides for the demolition of the remaining block walls from the previous dwelling on the site (remaining from works carried out under Reg. Ref. F11A/0007) and the construction of one four-bedroom, 2.5-storey detached residence with front and rear first-floor balconies, generous private gardens, off-street parking, new boundary treatments, landscaping and all associated site development works.\n\nDiscreetly positioned behind private gates within a quiet and exclusive cul-de-sac, the site enjoys a peaceful setting surrounded by mature trees and established gardens, offering exceptional privacy while remaining remarkably well connected.\n\nFew locations offer the balance of lifestyle and accessibility found in Howth. The picturesque harbour village, with its renowned restaurants, cafés, boutiques and marina, is just minutes away, while the nearby DART station provides regular services to Dublin City Centre. Dublin Airport, the M50 motorway and the city's principal business districts are all easily accessible, making Woodview an ideal choice for commuters and international buyers alike.\n\nHowth's enduring appeal lies not only in its spectacular coastal scenery but also in its exceptional range of amenities. Residents enjoy access to scenic cliff and coastal walks, beaches, sailing, golf, tennis, rugby, GAA and an abundance of recreational facilities, together with an excellent selection of highly regarded primary and secondary schools. It is a location that continues to attract families seeking an outstanding quality of life within easy reach of the capital.\n\nPlanning Reference: F25A/1012E (available to view on www.fingalcoco.ie).\n\nPlease note that the CGI image has been created using AI based on the architect's approved plans and is provided for illustrative purposes only. It is not to scale and should not be relied upon as an exact representation of the finished dwelling."
      },
      {
